      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The subgrade's stability is critical because uneven compaction creates weak points that fail under the repetitive stress of Phoenix's extreme thermal expansion and contraction. If the subgrade deflects excessively due to poor compaction, it can support the surface layer unevenly, causing localized bending that stresses the asphalt and accelerates thermal cracking. Ultimately, a compromised subgrade negates the benefits of a well-mixed surface layer, significantly reducing the pavement's overall design life in high-temperature environments.",
